@startuml obj_aura

package object {
  class ObjAura {
    -- Fields --
    - gameWindow: GameWindow
    - DIRECTIONS: String[] = {"Up","Down","Left","Right"}
    - FRAMES_PER_DIRECTION: int = 3
    - active: boolean
    - expireAt: long
    - elapsedMilliseconds: long
    - currentFrameIndexOneBased: int = 1
    - totalFrames: int = 3
    - FRAME_INTERVAL_MS: long = 1500L
    - sprites: BufferedImage[][]
    -- Methods --
    + ObjAura(gameWindow: GameWindow)
    - loadSpriteFrames(): void
    + getAnimationFrame(): BufferedImage
    + updateAnimation(deltaMs: long): void
    + drawAt(g2: Graphics2D, screenX: int, screenY: int, scale: float, alpha: float): void
    + activate(durationMs: long): void
    + deactivate(): void
    + isActive(): boolean
    + setActive(active: boolean): void
    + isActiveRaw(): boolean
    + getExpireAt(): long
    - createImage(original:BufferedImage, width:int, height:int): BufferedImage
  }
}

package frame {
  class FrameApp {
    + getTileSize(): int
    + getScreenWidth(): int
  }
}

package window {
  class GameWindow {
    + getPlayer(): Player
    + getUi(): UI
  }
  class UI {
    + setCurrentDialogueMessage(msg: String): void
  }
}

package entity {
  abstract class Entity {
    + getGameWindow(): GameWindow
    + setName(name: String): void
    + sprites: BufferedImage[][]
  }
}

ObjAura --> window.GameWindow : uses
ObjAura --> frame.FrameApp : queries
ObjAura --> entity.Entity : extends

note right of ObjAura
**Notes**
- スプライトフレームを読み込みタイルサイズにリサイズして保持する
- フレーム間隔でアニメを更新し有効期限で自動的に無効化する
- 指定スクリーン座標に拡大・アルファ合成で描画する
- activate で有効化し指定時間後に expireAt により無効化される

- Load sprite frames, resize them to the tile size, and store them.
- Update the animation based on frame intervals and automatically deactivate when the expiration time is reached.
- Render the animation at a specified screen position with scaling and alpha compositing.
- Activate the aura for a given duration; it becomes inactive after expireAt is reached.
end note

@enduml